There was talk on whether a Cursed amulet of life saving would have
the "soul-stealing effect" as described.

Actually, when you have a blessed amulet of life saving, when you
"die", you are restored to full hit points.

If it's uncursed, you just end up with a random amount, plus your
Con score.

BUT, if the amulet is cursed, yo DO get your life saved, and you will
be restored 1 hit point, ala the Scroll of Life Protection in LARN and
ULARN. When you HAVE one hit point, you might as well toss in the towel
and save yourself from an embarassing defeat and bones file.

Just tossing in my two zorkmids worth of advice.

